        "No pay-to-win. D$ is only earned by doing.": "Sin pagar para ganar. Los D$ solo se ganan haciendo.",
        "No selling your data.": "No vendemos tus datos.",
        "No manipulative streaks or fake urgency.": "Sin rachas manipuladoras ni urgencia falsa.",
        "Guided meditations, sound waves and a focus timer.": "Meditaciones guiadas, ondas de sonido y un temporizador de enfoque.",
        "Meditate & focus": "Meditar y enfocar",
        "11 guided meditations \xB7 sound waves \xB7 focus timer": "11 meditaciones guiadas \xB7 ondas de sonido \xB7 temporizador de enfoque",
        "Focus & meditations": "Enfoque y meditaciones",
        "Guided sessions and sound waves": "Sesiones guiadas y ondas de sonido",
        "Your future is built before breakfast or not at all.": "Tu futuro se construye antes del desayuno o no se construye.",
        "One kept promise to yourself outweighs a hundred plans.": "Una promesa cumplida a ti mismo pesa m\xE1s que cien planes.",
        "The life you want is on the other side of the task you avoid.": "La vida que quieres est\xE1 al otro lado de la tarea que evitas.",
        "Start before you feel ready. Readiness follows action.": "Empieza antes de sentirte listo. La preparaci\xF3n sigue a la acci\xF3n.",
        "Discipline is choosing the same future twice.": "La disciplina es elegir el mismo futuro dos veces.",
        "Today's ten minutes beat tomorrow's two hours.": "Diez minutos de hoy valen m\xE1s que dos horas de ma\xF1ana.",
        "You don't find time. You take it.": "El tiempo no se encuentra. Se toma.",
        "Small decisions, kept daily, become an unrecognizable life.": "Peque\xF1as decisiones, cumplidas a diario, se convierten en una vida irreconocible.",
        "Motivation is a visitor. Habit is a resident.": "La motivaci\xF3n es una visita. El h\xE1bito es un residente.",
        "The dream doesn't need you to be perfect. It needs you to show up.": "Tu sue\xF1o no necesita que seas perfecto. Necesita que aparezcas.",
        "Every avoided decision is a decision to stay.": "Cada decisi\xF3n evitada es una decisi\xF3n de quedarte donde est\xE1s.",
        "Do the hard thing first. The day gets lighter.": "Haz primero lo dif\xEDcil. El d\xEDa se vuelve m\xE1s ligero.",
        "You are always one decision away from a different day.": "Siempre est\xE1s a una decisi\xF3n de un d\xEDa diferente.",
        "What you repeat, you become.": "Te conviertes en lo que repites.",
        "Done today is stronger than perfect someday.": "Hecho hoy es m\xE1s fuerte que perfecto alg\xFAn d\xEDa.",
        "Quiet mornings build loud futures.": "Las ma\xF1anas silenciosas construyen futuros que se escuchan.",
        "Don't negotiate with the alarm. Negotiate with your future.": "No negocies con la alarma. Negocia con tu futuro.",
        "Effort compounds in silence.": "El esfuerzo se acumula en silencio.",
        "The version of you in three years is watching today.": "Tu versi\xF3n de dentro de tres a\xF1os est\xE1 mirando el d\xEDa de hoy.",
        "A focused hour is a vote for the life you said you wanted.": "Una hora de enfoque es un voto por la vida que dijiste querer.",
        "Comfort is expensive. It costs the future.": "La comodidad es cara. Cuesta el futuro.",
        "Begin. The bridge appears as you walk.": "Empieza. El puente aparece mientras caminas.",
        "Nobody is coming. That is the good news.": "Nadie va a venir. Esa es la buena noticia.",
        "Protect the first hour and the day protects itself.": "Protege la primera hora y el d\xEDa se protege solo.",
        "You can't think your way into a new life. You act your way there.": "No llegas a una vida nueva pensando. Llegas actuando.",
        "The task shrinks the moment you touch it.": "La tarea se encoge en cuanto la tocas.",
        "Keep the promise small enough to keep.": "Haz la promesa lo bastante peque\xF1a como para cumplirla.",
        "Rest is part of the work. Escape is not.": "Descansar es parte del trabajo. Escapar no.",
        "Direction beats speed. Choose, then walk.": "La direcci\xF3n vence a la velocidad. Elige y camina.",
        "Your habits are voting for a future. Check the ballot.": "Tus h\xE1bitos est\xE1n votando por un futuro. Revisa la papeleta.",
        "The excuse also takes energy. Spend it on the task.": "La excusa tambi\xE9n consume energ\xEDa. G\xE1stala en la tarea.",
        "One honest page beats a week of intentions.": "Una p\xE1gina honesta vale m\xE1s que una semana de intenciones.",
        "Show up on the gray days. That's where the gap closes.": "Aparece en los d\xEDas grises. Ah\xED es donde se cierra la brecha.",
        "The future doesn't arrive. It accumulates.": "El futuro no llega. Se acumula.",
        "Choose the discomfort that pays rent.": "Elige la incomodidad que paga renta.",
        "Waiting is also a habit. Break it like one.": "Esperar tambi\xE9n es un h\xE1bito. R\xF3mpelo como tal.",
        "Make it easy to start and hard to quit.": "Haz que empezar sea f\xE1cil y rendirse dif\xEDcil.",
        "A calm mind is a working tool, not a luxury.": "Una mente en calma es una herramienta de trabajo, no un lujo.",
        "Today is the oldest you've been and the youngest you'll be. Use it.": "Hoy es lo m\xE1s viejo que has sido y lo m\xE1s joven que ser\xE1s. \xDAsalo.",
        "Your attention is the currency. Spend it like money.": "Tu atenci\xF3n es la moneda. G\xE1stala como dinero.",
        "Finish something small before noon.": "Termina algo peque\xF1o antes del mediod\xEDa.",
        "The plan is not the work.": "El plan no es el trabajo.",
        "Doubt gets a vote, not a veto.": "La duda tiene voto, no veto.",
        "You water what you look at. Look at the dream.": "Riegas lo que miras. Mira tu sue\xF1o.",
        "Slow is fine. Stopped is the only failure.": "Ir despacio est\xE1 bien. Detenerse es el \xFAnico fracaso.",
        "Say no to the good so you can say yes to the built.": "Di no a lo bueno para poder decir s\xED a lo construido.",
        "Your environment is a decision you make once and obey daily.": "Tu entorno es una decisi\xF3n que tomas una vez y obedeces a diario.",
        "Act like the person you wrote about last night.": "Act\xFAa como la persona sobre la que escribiste anoche.",
        "The first rep is the decision. The rest is momentum.": "La primera repetici\xF3n es la decisi\xF3n. El resto es impulso.",
        "Don't count the days you missed. Count the one in front of you.": "No cuentes los d\xEDas que perdiste. Cuenta el que tienes delante.",
        "A short walk fixes more than a long scroll.": "Una caminata corta arregla m\xE1s que un scroll largo.",
        "Earn the evening.": "G\xE1nate la noche.",
        "Write it down. The mind is for deciding, not storing.": "Escr\xEDbelo. La mente es para decidir, no para almacenar.",
        "What scares you at 9 is done by 9:20 if you start at 9.": "Lo que te asusta a las 9 est\xE1 hecho a las 9:20 si empiezas a las 9.",
        "Consistency looks boring for weeks and unbelievable in a year.": "La constancia parece aburrida durante semanas e incre\xEDble en un a\xF1o.",
        "You built today's normal. You can build a different one.": "T\xFA construiste lo normal de hoy. Puedes construir otro distinto.",
        "Ask less of the mood and more of the calendar.": "P\xEDdele menos al \xE1nimo y m\xE1s al calendario.",
        "The distance between you and the dream is measured in kept days.": "La distancia entre t\xFA y el sue\xF1o se mide en d\xEDas cumplidos.",
        "Decide once, in the morning, and let the day obey.": "Decide una vez, por la ma\xF1ana, y deja que el d\xEDa obedezca.",
        "Indeed, with hardship comes ease.": "Ciertamente, junto a la dificultad hay facilidad.",
        "Quran 94:6": "Cor\xE1n 94:6",
        "God does not change the condition of a people until they change what is in themselves.": "Dios no cambia la condici\xF3n de un pueblo hasta que ellos cambian lo que hay en s\xED mismos.",
        "Quran 13:11": "Cor\xE1n 13:11",
        "Man shall have nothing but what he strives for.": "El ser humano solo obtendr\xE1 aquello por lo que se esfuerza.",
        "Quran 53:39": "Cor\xE1n 53:39",
        "God does not burden a soul beyond what it can bear.": "Dios no impone a nadie una carga mayor de la que puede soportar.",
        "Quran 2:286": "Cor\xE1n 2:286",
        "Do not despair of the mercy of God.": "No desesper\xE9is de la misericordia de Dios.",
        "Quran 39:53": "Cor\xE1n 39:53",
        "Whoever puts their trust in God \u2014 He is enough for them.": "Quien conf\xEDa en Dios, \xC9l le basta.",
        "Quran 65:3": "Cor\xE1n 65:3",
        "Seek help through patience and prayer.": "Buscad ayuda en la paciencia y la oraci\xF3n.",
        "Quran 2:153": "Cor\xE1n 2:153",
        "Those who strive for Us \u2014 We will surely guide them to Our ways.": "A quienes se esfuerzan por Nosotros, los guiaremos por Nuestros caminos.",
        "Quran 29:69": "Cor\xE1n 29:69",
        "Do not lose hope, nor be sad.": "No os desanim\xE9is ni os entristezc\xE1is.",
        "Quran 3:139": "Cor\xE1n 3:139",
        "Say: My Lord, increase me in knowledge.": "Di: Se\xF1or m\xEDo, aum\xE9ntame en conocimiento.",
        "Quran 20:114": "Cor\xE1n 20:114",
        "When you have decided, put your trust in God.": "Cuando hayas decidido, conf\xEDa en Dios.",
        "Quran 3:159": "Cor\xE1n 3:159",
        "Be patient; indeed, the promise of God is truth.": "S\xE9 paciente; la promesa de Dios es verdadera.",
        "Quran 30:60": "Cor\xE1n 30:60",
        "If you are grateful, I will surely increase you.": "Si sois agradecidos, os dar\xE9 a\xFAn m\xE1s.",
        "Quran 14:7": "Cor\xE1n 14:7",
        "God is with the patient.": "Dios est\xE1 con los pacientes.",
        "By time, surely mankind is in loss \u2014 except those who believe and do good.": "Por el tiempo, el ser humano est\xE1 en p\xE9rdida, salvo quienes creen y obran el bien.",
        "Quran 103:1-3": "Cor\xE1n 103:1-3",
        "Remember Me, and I will remember you.": "Acordaos de M\xED, que Yo me acordar\xE9 de vosotros.",
        "Quran 2:152": "Cor\xE1n 2:152",
        "My success is only through God.": "Mi \xE9xito solo viene de Dios.",
        "Quran 11:88": "Cor\xE1n 11:88",
        "Hearts find rest in the remembrance of God.": "Los corazones se sosiegan con el recuerdo de Dios.",
        "Quran 13:28": "Cor\xE1n 13:28",
        "Whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it.": "Quien haga el bien, aunque sea del peso de un \xE1tomo, lo ver\xE1.",
        "Quran 99:7": "Cor\xE1n 99:7",
        "Your Lord has not forsaken you, nor does He hate you. The future will be better for you than the past.": "Tu Se\xF1or no te ha abandonado ni te aborrece. El porvenir ser\xE1 mejor para ti que el pasado.",
        "Quran 93:3-4": "Cor\xE1n 93:3-4",
        "Walk the earth and eat of His provision \u2014 to Him is the resurrection.": "Recorred la tierra y comed de Su sustento.",
        "Quran 67:15": "Cor\xE1n 67:15",
        "When the prayer is ended, disperse in the land and seek the bounty of God.": "Terminada la oraci\xF3n, dispersaos por la tierra y buscad el favor de Dios.",
        "Quran 62:10": "Cor\xE1n 62:10",
        "Speak to people with kindness.": "Hablad a la gente con bondad.",
        "Quran 2:83": "Cor\xE1n 2:83",
        "Repel evil with what is better.": "Responde al mal con lo que es mejor.",
        "Quran 41:34": "Cor\xE1n 41:34",
        "Do not walk upon the earth with arrogance.": "No camines por la tierra con arrogancia.",
        "Quran 17:37": "Cor\xE1n 17:37",
        "Indeed, God loves those who rely upon Him.": "Dios ama a quienes conf\xEDan en \xC9l.",
        "Be just; that is nearer to righteousness.": "Sed justos: eso est\xE1 m\xE1s cerca de la rectitud.",
        "Quran 5:8": "Cor\xE1n 5:8",
        "Give the relative his right, and the poor and the traveler.": "Da su derecho al pariente, al pobre y al viajero.",
        "Quran 17:26": "Cor\xE1n 17:26",
        "And He found you lost and guided you.": "\xBFNo te hall\xF3 extraviado y te guio?",
        "Quran 93:7": "Cor\xE1n 93:7",
        "So when you are free, labor on, and to your Lord direct your longing.": "Cuando termines una tarea, emprende otra, y dirige tu anhelo a tu Se\xF1or.",
        "Quran 94:7-8": "Cor\xE1n 94:7-8",
        "Waste no more time arguing what a good man should be. Be one.": "No pierdas m\xE1s tiempo discutiendo c\xF3mo debe ser un buen hombre. S\xE9 uno.",
        "Marcus Aurelius": "Marco Aurelio",
        "You have power over your mind, not outside events. Realize this, and you will find strength.": "Tienes poder sobre tu mente, no sobre los acontecimientos. Comprende esto y hallar\xE1s fuerza.",
        "It is not that we have a short time to live, but that we waste much of it.": "No es que tengamos poco tiempo, sino que desperdiciamos mucho.",
        "Seneca": "S\xE9neca",
        "Luck is what happens when preparation meets opportunity.": "La suerte es lo que ocurre cuando la preparaci\xF3n se encuentra con la oportunidad.",
        "Begin at once to live, and count each separate day as a separate life.": "Empieza a vivir de inmediato y cuenta cada d\xEDa como una vida aparte.",
        "No man is free who is not master of himself.": "Ning\xFAn hombre es libre si no es due\xF1o de s\xED mismo.",
        "Epictetus": "Epicteto",
        "First say to yourself what you would be; and then do what you have to do.": "Primero dite a ti mismo lo que quieres ser; luego haz lo que debes hacer.",
        "Yesterday I was clever, so I wanted to change the world. Today I am wise, so I am changing myself.": "Ayer era listo y quer\xEDa cambiar el mundo. Hoy soy sabio y me estoy cambiando a m\xED mismo.",
        "Rumi": "Rumi",
        "As you start to walk on the way, the way appears.": "Cuando empiezas a andar el camino, el camino aparece.",
        "Either exist as you are, or be as you look.": "O mu\xE9strate como eres, o s\xE9 como te muestras.",
        "Patience is the key to joy.": "La paciencia es la llave de la alegr\xEDa.",
        "It does not matter how slowly you go as long as you do not stop.": "No importa lo despacio que vayas mientras no te detengas.",
        "Confucius": "Confucio",
        "The man who moves a mountain begins by carrying away small stones.": "El hombre que mueve una monta\xF1a comienza cargando piedras peque\xF1as.",
        "When it is obvious that the goals cannot be reached, don't adjust the goals; adjust the action steps.": "Si es evidente que no alcanzas la meta, no ajustes la meta: ajusta los pasos.",
        "A journey of a thousand miles begins with a single step.": "Un viaje de mil millas comienza con un solo paso.",
        "Lao Tzu": "Lao Tse",
        "He who conquers others is strong; he who conquers himself is mighty.": "Quien vence a otros es fuerte; quien se vence a s\xED mismo es poderoso.",
        "We are what we repeatedly do. Excellence, then, is not an act, but a habit.": "Somos lo que hacemos repetidamente. La excelencia no es un acto, sino un h\xE1bito.",
        "Aristotle": "Arist\xF3teles",
        "Through discipline comes freedom.": "A trav\xE9s de la disciplina llega la libertad.",
        "The beginning is the most important part of the work.": "El comienzo es la parte m\xE1s importante de la obra.",
        "Plato": "Plat\xF3n",
        "An unexamined life is not worth living.": "Una vida sin examen no merece ser vivida.",
        "Socrates": "S\xF3crates",
        "Knowing yourself is the beginning of all wisdom.": "Conocerte a ti mismo es el principio de toda sabidur\xEDa.",
        "What you seek is seeking you.": "Lo que buscas te est\xE1 buscando.",
        "Come, come, whoever you are. Ours is not a caravan of despair.": "Ven, ven, seas quien seas. Nuestra caravana no es la de la desesperanza.",
        "Let the beauty of what you love be what you do.": "Que la belleza de lo que amas sea lo que haces.",
        "Knowledge is knowing yourself.": "El conocimiento es conocerse a uno mismo.",
        "Yunus Emre": "Yunus Emre",
        "Let us know one another; the world will remain to no one.": "Conozc\xE1monos unos a otros: el mundo no le quedar\xE1 a nadie.",
        "He who has no patience has no wisdom.": "Quien no tiene paciencia no tiene sabidur\xEDa.",
        "Saadi": "Saadi",
        "Have patience. All things are difficult before they become easy.": "Ten paciencia. Todo es dif\xEDcil antes de volverse f\xE1cil.",
        "Doubt is the origin of wisdom.": "La duda es el origen de la sabidur\xEDa.",
        "Descartes": "Descartes",
        "It is not enough to have a good mind; the main thing is to use it well.": "No basta con tener buen ingenio; lo principal es usarlo bien.",
        "He who is not courageous enough to take risks will accomplish nothing in life.": "Quien no tiene el valor de arriesgar no lograr\xE1 nada en la vida.",
        "Ibn Khaldun": "Ibn Jald\xFAn",
        "The past resembles the future more than one drop of water resembles another.": "El pasado se parece al futuro m\xE1s de lo que una gota de agua se parece a otra.",
        "Knowledge without action is madness, and action without knowledge is vanity.": "El conocimiento sin acci\xF3n es locura, y la acci\xF3n sin conocimiento, vanidad.",
        "Al-Ghazali": "Al-Ghazali",
        "Well begun is half done.": "Lo bien empezado est\xE1 a medio hacer.",
        "Do not wait to strike till the iron is hot; make it hot by striking.": "No esperes a que el hierro est\xE9 caliente para golpear; cali\xE9ntalo golpeando.",
        "W. B. Yeats": "W. B. Yeats",
        "Lost time is never found again.": "El tiempo perdido nunca se recupera.",
        "Benjamin Franklin": "Benjamin Franklin",
        "Energy and persistence conquer all things.": "La energ\xEDa y la constancia lo vencen todo.",
        "Knowing is not enough; we must apply. Willing is not enough; we must do.": "Saber no basta: hay que aplicar. Querer no basta: hay que hacer.",
        "Goethe": "Goethe",
        "Whatever you can do, or dream you can, begin it. Boldness has genius, power, and magic in it.": "Lo que puedas hacer o so\xF1ar, empi\xE9zalo. La audacia tiene genio, poder y magia.",
        "Nietzsche": "Nietzsche",
        "That which does not kill us makes us stronger.": "Lo que no nos mata nos hace m\xE1s fuertes.",
        "Everyone thinks of changing the world, but no one thinks of changing himself.": "Todos piensan en cambiar el mundo, pero nadie piensa en cambiarse a s\xED mismo.",
        "Tolstoy": "Tolst\xF3i",
        "The two most powerful warriors are patience and time.": "Los dos guerreros m\xE1s poderosos son la paciencia y el tiempo.",
        "It had long since come to my attention that people of accomplishment rarely sat back and let things happen to them. They went out and happened to things.": "Hace tiempo not\xE9 que la gente que logra cosas no espera a que le sucedan: sale y les sucede a las cosas.",
        "Leonardo da Vinci": "Leonardo da Vinci",
        "Simplicity is the ultimate sophistication.": "La sencillez es la m\xE1xima sofisticaci\xF3n.",
        "Plutarch": "Plutarco",
        "Success is not final, failure is not fatal: it is the courage to continue that counts.": "El \xE9xito no es definitivo ni el fracaso es fatal: lo que cuenta es el valor de continuar.",
        "Winston Churchill": "Winston Churchill",
        "The best way to predict the future is to create it.": "La mejor manera de predecir el futuro es crearlo.",
        "Abraham Lincoln": "Abraham Lincoln",
        "What lies behind us and what lies before us are tiny matters compared to what lies within us.": "Lo que queda atr\xE1s y lo que est\xE1 por venir son poca cosa comparado con lo que llevamos dentro.",
        "Emerson": "Emerson",
        "Do not go where the path may lead; go instead where there is no path and leave a trail.": "No vayas por donde lleve el camino; ve por donde no hay camino y deja huella.",
        "Go confidently in the direction of your dreams. Live the life you have imagined.": "Avanza con confianza en la direcci\xF3n de tus sue\xF1os. Vive la vida que imaginaste.",
        "Thoreau": "Thoreau",
        "If one advances confidently toward his dreams, he will meet with a success unexpected in common hours.": "Quien avanza con confianza hacia sus sue\xF1os encuentra un \xE9xito inesperado en las horas comunes.",
        "There is nothing impossible to him who will try.": "Nada es imposible para quien lo intenta.",
        "Alexander the Great": "Alejandro Magno",
        "A goal without a plan is just a wish.": "Una meta sin plan es solo un deseo.",
        "Antoine de Saint-Exup\xE9ry": "Antoine de Saint-Exup\xE9ry",
        "The day you plant the seed is not the day you eat the fruit. Plant anyway.": "El d\xEDa que plantas la semilla no es el d\xEDa que comes el fruto. Planta igualmente.",
        "Courage is a decision repeated quietly every morning.": "El valor es una decisi\xF3n que se repite en silencio cada ma\xF1ana.",
        "Your dream has a price in days. Start paying.": "Tu sue\xF1o tiene un precio en d\xEDas. Empieza a pagarlo.",
        "Read a page, walk a mile, keep a word. That is a good day.": "Lee una p\xE1gina, camina un rato, cumple una palabra. Eso es un buen d\xEDa.",
        "The mountain is climbed by the one who is still walking at noon.": "La monta\xF1a la sube quien sigue caminando al mediod\xEDa.",
        "If I have seen further, it is by standing on the shoulders of giants.": "Si he visto m\xE1s lejos, es porque estaba sobre hombros de gigantes.",
        "Isaac Newton": "Isaac Newton",
        "Genius is one percent inspiration and ninety-nine percent perspiration.": "El genio es un uno por ciento de inspiraci\xF3n y un noventa y nueve por ciento de transpiraci\xF3n.",
        "Thomas Edison": "Thomas Edison",
        "I have not failed. I've just found ten thousand ways that won't work.": "No he fracasado. Solo he encontrado diez mil maneras que no funcionan.",
        "Nothing in life is to be feared, it is only to be understood.": "Nada en la vida debe temerse, solo comprenderse.",
        "Marie Curie": "Marie Curie",
        "Be less curious about people and more curious about ideas.": "S\xE9 menos curioso sobre las personas y m\xE1s sobre las ideas.",
        "Life is like riding a bicycle. To keep your balance, you must keep moving.": "La vida es como andar en bicicleta. Para mantener el equilibrio, debes seguir avanzando.",
        "Albert Einstein": "Albert Einstein",
        "In the middle of difficulty lies opportunity.": "En medio de la dificultad se encuentra la oportunidad.",
        "Imagination is more important than knowledge.": "La imaginaci\xF3n es m\xE1s importante que el conocimiento.",
        "The present is theirs; the future, for which I really worked, is mine.": "El presente es de ellos; el futuro, por el que realmente trabaj\xE9, es m\xEDo.",
        "Nikola Tesla": "Nikola Tesla",
        "Chance favors the prepared mind.": "El azar favorece a la mente preparada.",
        "Louis Pasteur": "Louis Pasteur",
        "Nothing is too wonderful to be true, if it be consistent with the laws of nature.": "Nada es demasiado maravilloso para ser verdad si es coherente con las leyes de la naturaleza.",
        "Michael Faraday": "Michael Faraday",
        "It is not the strongest of the species that survives, but the one most responsive to change.": "No sobrevive la especie m\xE1s fuerte, sino la que mejor responde al cambio.",
        "Charles Darwin": "Charles Darwin",
        "Measure what is measurable, and make measurable what is not so.": "Mide lo que se pueda medir, y haz medible lo que no lo sea.",
        "Galileo Galilei": "Galileo Galilei",
        "Give me a place to stand, and I will move the earth.": "Dadme un punto de apoyo y mover\xE9 el mundo.",
        "Archimedes": "Arqu\xEDmedes",
        "Knowledge is the treasure, and practice is the key to it.": "El conocimiento es el tesoro y la pr\xE1ctica es su llave.",
        "Ibn Sina": "Avicena",
        "The width of life is more important than its length.": "La anchura de la vida importa m\xE1s que su longitud.",
        "Science is the great antidote to the poison of ignorance.": "La ciencia es el gran ant\xEDdoto contra el veneno de la ignorancia.",
        "Adam Smith": "Adam Smith",
        "Be the change that you wish to see in the world.": "S\xE9 el cambio que deseas ver en el mundo.",
        "Mahatma Gandhi": "Mahatma Gandhi",
        "Strength does not come from physical capacity. It comes from an indomitable will.": "La fuerza no viene de la capacidad f\xEDsica, sino de una voluntad indomable.",
        "Live as if you were to die tomorrow. Learn as if you were to live forever.": "Vive como si fueras a morir ma\xF1ana. Aprende como si fueras a vivir para siempre.",
        "It always seems impossible until it is done.": "Siempre parece imposible hasta que se hace.",
        "Nelson Mandela": "Nelson Mandela",
        "I never lose. I either win or learn.": "Nunca pierdo. O gano o aprendo.",
        "Do not judge me by my successes; judge me by how many times I fell down and got back up again.": "No me juzgues por mis \xE9xitos, sino por cu\xE1ntas veces ca\xED y volv\xED a levantarme.",
        "You cannot cross the sea merely by standing and staring at the water.": "No puedes cruzar el mar solo mirando el agua.",
        "Rabindranath Tagore": "Rabindranath Tagore",
        "Faith is the bird that feels the light when the dawn is still dark.": "La fe es el p\xE1jaro que siente la luz cuando el alba a\xFAn est\xE1 oscura.",
        "If you can't fly then run, if you can't run then walk, if you can't walk then crawl, but by all means keep moving.": "Si no puedes volar, corre; si no puedes correr, camina; si no puedes caminar, gatea; pero, hagas lo que hagas, sigue avanzando.",
        "Martin Luther King Jr.": "Martin Luther King Jr.",
        "Faith is taking the first step even when you don't see the whole staircase.": "La fe es dar el primer paso aunque no veas toda la escalera.",
        "The darkest hour has only sixty minutes.": "La hora m\xE1s oscura solo tiene sesenta minutos.",
        "Morris Mandel": "Morris Mandel",
        "Turn your face to the sun and the shadows fall behind you.": "Vuelve tu rostro hacia el sol y las sombras quedar\xE1n detr\xE1s de ti.",
        "Maori proverb": "Proverbio maor\xED",
        "Fall seven times, stand up eight.": "Cae siete veces, lev\xE1ntate ocho.",
        "Japanese proverb": "Proverbio japon\xE9s",
        "The best time to plant a tree was twenty years ago. The second best time is now.": "El mejor momento para plantar un \xE1rbol fue hace veinte a\xF1os. El segundo mejor momento es ahora.",
        "Chinese proverb": "Proverbio chino",
        "If you want to go fast, go alone. If you want to go far, go together.": "Si quieres ir r\xE1pido, ve solo. Si quieres llegar lejos, ve acompa\xF1ado.",
        "African proverb": "Proverbio africano",
        "However long the night, the dawn will break.": "Por larga que sea la noche, amanecer\xE1.",
        "A smooth sea never made a skilled sailor.": "Un mar en calma nunca hizo a un marinero experto.",
        "English proverb": "Proverbio ingl\xE9s",
        "Little by little, the bird builds its nest.": "Poco a poco, el p\xE1jaro hace su nido.",
        "French proverb": "Proverbio franc\xE9s",
        "He who rises early, God helps.": "A quien madruga, Dios lo ayuda.",
        "Spanish proverb": "Proverbio espa\xF1ol",
        "Damlaya damlaya g\xF6l olur \u2014 drop by drop, a lake is formed.": "Gota a gota se forma el lago.",
        "Turkish proverb": "Proverbio turco",
        "The one who walks the road learns more than the one who reads about it.": "Quien camina el camino aprende m\xE1s que quien lee sobre \xE9l.",
        "Anatolian saying": "Dicho de Anatolia",
        "Science is the most genuine guide in life.": "La ciencia es la gu\xEDa m\xE1s verdadera en la vida.",
        "Mustafa Kemal Atat\xFCrk": "Mustafa Kemal Atat\xFCrk",
        "Hope is the pillar that holds up the world.": "La esperanza es el pilar que sostiene el mundo.",
        "Pliny the Elder": "Plinio el Viejo",
        "They can because they think they can.": "Pueden porque creen que pueden.",
        "Virgil": "Virgilio",
        "Fortune favors the bold.": "La fortuna favorece a los audaces.",
        "Carpe diem \u2014 seize the day.": "Carpe diem: aprovecha el d\xEDa.",
        "Horace": "Horacio",
        "He who is brave is free.": "Quien es valiente es libre.",
        "Man is affected not by events but by the view he takes of them.": "Al hombre no lo afectan los hechos, sino la manera en que los mira.",
        "Do every act of your life as though it were the very last act of your life.": "Haz cada acto de tu vida como si fuera el \xFAltimo.",
        "Very little is needed to make a happy life; it is all within yourself.": "Se necesita muy poco para una vida feliz; todo est\xE1 dentro de ti.",
        "Pray as if everything depends on God; work as if everything depends on you.": "Reza como si todo dependiera de Dios; trabaja como si todo dependiera de ti.",
        "Augustine of Hippo": "San Agust\xEDn",
        "Trust in God, but tie your camel.": "Conf\xEDa en Dios, pero ata tu camello.",
        "Prophetic wisdom": "Sabidur\xEDa prof\xE9tica",
        "Actions are judged by intentions.": "Las acciones se juzgan por las intenciones.",
        "The strong is not the one who overcomes people; the strong is the one who controls himself in anger.": "El fuerte no es quien vence a los dem\xE1s, sino quien se domina a s\xED mismo en la ira.",
        "The most beloved deeds to God are those done regularly, even if small.": "Las obras m\xE1s amadas por Dios son las constantes, aunque sean peque\xF1as.",
        "This world is the field of the hereafter: what you sow here, you harvest there.": "Este mundo es el campo de la otra vida: lo que siembras aqu\xED, lo cosechas all\xE1.",
        "Islamic wisdom": "Sabidur\xEDa isl\xE1mica",
        "Whoever saves himself from his own greed \u2014 those are the successful.": "Quienes se libran de su propia avaricia, esos son los que prosperan.",
        "Quran 59:9": "Cor\xE1n 59:9",
        "God is the light of the heavens and the earth.": "Dios es la luz de los cielos y de la tierra.",
        "Quran 24:35": "Cor\xE1n 24:35",
        "Call upon Me; I will respond to you.": "Invocadme, y os responder\xE9.",
        "Quran 40:60": "Cor\xE1n 40:60",
        "It may be that you dislike a thing and it is good for you.": "Puede que os disguste algo que es un bien para vosotros.",
        "Quran 2:216": "Cor\xE1n 2:216",
        "And your Lord is going to give you, and you will be satisfied.": "Tu Se\xF1or te dar\xE1 y quedar\xE1s satisfecho.",
        "Quran 93:5": "Cor\xE1n 93:5",
        "Peace begins with a smile.": "La paz comienza con una sonrisa.",
        "Mother Teresa": "Madre Teresa",
        "Not all of us can do great things. But we can do small things with great love.": "No todos podemos hacer grandes cosas, pero s\xED cosas peque\xF1as con un gran amor.",
        "Where there is no vision, the people perish.": "Donde no hay visi\xF3n, el pueblo perece.",
        "Proverbs 29:18": "Proverbios 29:18",
        "Whatever your hand finds to do, do it with all your might.": "Todo lo que tu mano encuentre para hacer, hazlo con todas tus fuerzas.",
        "Ecclesiastes 9:10": "Eclesiast\xE9s 9:10",
        "The energy of the mind is the essence of life.": "La energ\xEDa de la mente es la esencia de la vida.",
        "Where attention goes, energy flows.": "Donde va la atenci\xF3n, fluye la energ\xEDa.",
        "Huna wisdom": "Sabidur\xEDa huna",
        "What you think, you become. What you feel, you attract.": "En lo que piensas te conviertes; lo que sientes lo atraes.",
        "Buddhist wisdom": "Sabidur\xEDa budista",
        "The mind is everything.": "La mente lo es todo.",
        "Each morning we are born again. What we do today is what matters most.": "Cada ma\xF1ana nacemos de nuevo. Lo que hacemos hoy es lo que m\xE1s importa.",
        "Drop by drop is the water pot filled.": "Gota a gota se llena el c\xE1ntaro.",
        "A man is but the product of his thoughts; what he thinks, he becomes.": "El hombre es producto de sus pensamientos; en lo que piensa, se convierte.",
        "Be patient, outdo one another in patience, and remain steadfast, so that you may succeed.": "S\xE9 paciente, supera a otros en paciencia y mantente firme, para que triunfes.",
        "Quran 3:200": "Cor\xE1n 3:200",
        "God is enough for us, and He is the best guardian of our affairs.": "Dios nos basta, y \xC9l es el mejor protector de nuestros asuntos.",
        "Quran 3:173": "Cor\xE1n 3:173",
        "Do not grieve; indeed, God is with us.": "No te aflijas; ciertamente, Dios est\xE1 con nosotros.",
        "Quran 9:40": "Cor\xE1n 9:40",
        "I am near \u2014 I answer the call of the one who calls on Me.": "Estoy cerca: respondo a la llamada de quien Me invoca.",
        "Quran 2:186": "Cor\xE1n 2:186",
        "Whoever does good, man or woman, while believing \u2014 We will surely give them a good life.": "A quien haga el bien, hombre o mujer, siendo creyente, le daremos una vida buena.",
        "Quran 16:97": "Cor\xE1n 16:97",
        "Keep up the prayer, encourage what is right, and be patient with whatever befalls you.": "Mant\xE9n la oraci\xF3n, anima al bien y s\xE9 paciente con lo que te suceda.",
        "Quran 31:17": "Cor\xE1n 31:17",
        "Whoever is patient and forgives \u2014 that is true strength of resolve.": "Quien es paciente y perdona muestra la verdadera firmeza de \xE1nimo.",
        "Quran 42:43": "Cor\xE1n 42:43",
        "He is with you wherever you are.": "\xC9l est\xE1 contigo dondequiera que est\xE9s.",
        "Quran 57:4": "Cor\xE1n 57:4",
        "Do not grieve over what has passed you by, nor gloat over what you have been given.": "No te aflijas por lo que perdiste ni te envanezcas por lo que recibiste.",
        "Quran 57:23": "Cor\xE1n 57:23",
        "Whoever believes in God \u2014 He guides their heart.": "A quien cree en Dios, \xC9l le gu\xEDa el coraz\xF3n.",
        "Quran 64:11": "Cor\xE1n 64:11",
        "Be patient, for God does not let the reward of those who do good be lost.": "S\xE9 paciente, pues Dios no deja perderse la recompensa de quienes hacen el bien.",
        "Quran 11:115": "Cor\xE1n 11:115",
        "The servants of the Merciful walk the earth humbly, and when the ignorant address them, they answer: Peace.": "Los siervos del Misericordioso caminan con humildad, y cuando los ignorantes les hablan, responden: Paz.",
        "Quran 25:63": "Cor\xE1n 25:63",
        "Seek the life to come in what God has given you, but do not forget your share of this world.": "Busca la vida venidera con lo que Dios te ha dado, pero no olvides tu parte en este mundo.",
        "Quran 28:77": "Cor\xE1n 28:77",
        "Is the reward for good anything but good?": "\xBFAcaso la recompensa del bien puede ser otra cosa que el bien?",
        "Quran 55:60": "Cor\xE1n 55:60",
        "If you do good, you do it for yourself.": "Si haces el bien, te lo haces a ti mismo.",
        "Quran 17:7": "Cor\xE1n 17:7",
        "Do good; truly God loves those who do good.": "Haz el bien; en verdad Dios ama a los que hacen el bien.",
        "Quran 2:195": "Cor\xE1n 2:195",
        "Those who are patient will be given their reward without measure.": "A los pacientes se les dar\xE1 su recompensa sin medida.",
        "Quran 39:10": "Cor\xE1n 39:10",
        "Those who restrain their anger and pardon people \u2014 God loves those who do good.": "Quienes contienen su ira y perdonan a la gente: Dios ama a los que hacen el bien.",
        "Quran 3:134": "Cor\xE1n 3:134",
        "Truly successful is the one who purifies the soul.": "En verdad triunfa quien purifica su alma.",
        "Quran 91:9": "Cor\xE1n 91:9",
        "If you tried to count the blessings of God, you could never number them.": "Si intentaras contar las bendiciones de Dios, no podr\xEDas enumerarlas.",
        "Quran 16:18": "Cor\xE1n 16:18",
        "Make things easy, do not make them hard; give good news, do not drive people away.": "Facilita, no dificultes; anuncia lo bueno, no alejes a la gente.",
        "The best of people are those most helpful to people.": "Los mejores entre las personas son quienes m\xE1s ayudan a los dem\xE1s.",
        "Value your health before illness and your free time before it is filled.": "Valora tu salud antes de la enfermedad y tu tiempo libre antes de que se llene.",
        "God loves that when you do a piece of work, you do it well.": "Dios ama que, cuando hagas un trabajo, lo hagas bien.",
        "Richness is not having many possessions; richness is contentment of the soul.": "La riqueza no es tener mucho; la verdadera riqueza es la serenidad del alma.",
        "Be in this world as if you were a traveler passing along a road.": "Est\xE1 en este mundo como un viajero que pasa por un camino.",
        "A kind word is charity.": "Una palabra amable es una obra de caridad.",
        "Whoever walks a path in search of knowledge, God eases their way.": "A quien recorre un camino en busca de conocimiento, Dios le facilita la senda.",
        "If the end of the world comes while you hold a sapling in your hand, plant it.": "Si llega el fin del mundo y tienes un reto\xF1o en la mano, pl\xE1ntalo.",
        "Do not let hardship fill you with despair; stars shine brightest in the darkest night.": "No dejes que la dificultad te llene de desesperanza; las estrellas brillan m\xE1s en la noche m\xE1s oscura.",
        "Ali ibn Abi Talib": "Ali ibn Abi Talib",
        "Patience is of two kinds: patience over what pains you, and patience against what you crave.": "La paciencia es de dos clases: paciencia ante lo que duele y paciencia frente a lo que deseas.",
        "Do not be a slave to another when God has created you free.": "No seas esclavo de nadie, pues Dios te cre\xF3 libre.",
        "Your cure is within you, though you do not see it.": "Tu remedio est\xE1 dentro de ti, aunque no lo veas.",
        "Hold yourself to account before you are held to account.": "R\xEDndete cuentas a ti mismo antes de que te las pidan.",
        "Omar ibn al-Khattab": "Omar ibn al-Jattab",
        "The most beloved to me is the one who shows me my faults.": "La persona m\xE1s querida para m\xED es la que me muestra mis defectos.",
        "The words you speak become the house you live in.": "Las palabras que dices se convierten en la casa donde vives.",
        "Hafiz": "Hafiz",
        "Be happy for this moment. This moment is your life.": "S\xE9 feliz en este momento; este momento es tu vida.",
        "Omar Khayyam": "Omar Jayam",
        "The ocean can be yours; why should you settle for a drop of dew?": "El oc\xE9ano puede ser tuyo; \xBFpor qu\xE9 conformarte con una gota de roc\xEDo?",
        "Attar": "Attar",
        "Strive to discover the mystery before life is taken from you.": "Esfu\xE9rzate por descubrir el misterio antes de que la vida se te escape.",
        "He who knows himself knows his Lord.": "Quien se conoce a s\xED mismo, conoce a su Se\xF1or.",
        "Ibn Arabi": "Ibn Arabi",
        "A candle loses nothing by lighting another candle.": "Una vela no pierde nada por encender otra vela.",
        "Shams Tabrizi": "Shams de Tabriz",
        "Wherever you are, that is the entry point.": "Dondequiera que est\xE9s, ese es el punto de entrada.",
        "Kabir": "Kabir",
        "The river that flows in you also flows in me.": "El r\xEDo que fluye en ti tambi\xE9n fluye en m\xED.",
        "Do not go looking for the garden of flowers; the garden is within you.": "No salgas a buscar el jard\xEDn de flores; el jard\xEDn est\xE1 dentro de ti.",
        "Raise your words, not your voice. It is rain that grows flowers, not thunder.": "Eleva tus palabras, no tu voz; es la lluvia la que hace crecer las flores, no el trueno.",
        "You are not a drop in the ocean; you are the entire ocean in a drop.": "No eres una gota en el oc\xE9ano; eres el oc\xE9ano entero en una gota.",
        "Yesterday is gone and took its story with it; today, sow new seeds.": "El ayer se fue y se llev\xF3 su historia; hoy siembra semillas nuevas.",
        "A traveler without knowledge is a bird without wings.": "Un viajero sin conocimiento es un p\xE1jaro sin alas.",
        "Whatever is made in haste is easily undone.": "Lo que se hace con prisa se deshace con facilidad.",
        "A little and a little, gathered together, become a great deal.": "Poco a poco, lo reunido llega a ser mucho.",
        "While we are postponing, life speeds by.": "Mientras aplazamos, la vida pasa de largo.",
        "If you do not know to which port you are sailing, no wind is favorable.": "Si no sabes a qu\xE9 puerto navegas, ning\xFAn viento te es favorable.",
        "Difficulties strengthen the mind, as labor does the body.": "Las dificultades fortalecen la mente, como el trabajo fortalece el cuerpo.",
        "As long as you live, keep learning how to live.": "Mientras vivas, sigue aprendiendo a vivir.",
        "No great thing is created suddenly, any more than a bunch of grapes or a fig.": "Ninguna gran cosa se crea de repente, igual que un racimo de uvas o un higo.",
        "Do not explain your philosophy. Embody it.": "No expliques tu filosof\xEDa; enc\xE1rnala.",
        "Circumstances do not make the man; they reveal him to himself.": "Las circunstancias no hacen al hombre; se lo revelan a s\xED mismo.",
        "The happiness of your life depends upon the quality of your thoughts.": "La felicidad de tu vida depende de la calidad de tus pensamientos.",
        "Confine yourself to the present.": "C\xED\xF1ete al presente.",
        "If it is not right, do not do it; if it is not true, do not say it.": "Si no es correcto, no lo hagas; si no es verdad, no lo digas.",
        "When you arise in the morning, think of what a precious privilege it is to be alive.": "Al levantarte por la ma\xF1ana, piensa en el precioso privilegio de estar vivo.",
        "Dwell on the beauty of life. Watch the stars, and see yourself running with them.": "Contempla la belleza de la vida; mira las estrellas y corre con ellas.",
        "Gratitude is not only the greatest of virtues but the parent of all the others.": "La gratitud no solo es la mayor de las virtudes, sino la madre de todas las dem\xE1s.",
        "Cicero": "Cicer\xF3n",
        "While there is life, there is hope.": "Mientras hay vida, hay esperanza.",
        "An angry man opens his mouth and shuts his eyes.": "El hombre enojado abre la boca y cierra los ojos.",
        "Cato": "Cat\xF3n",
        "He has the most who is most content with the least.": "Quien m\xE1s se contenta con lo menos es quien m\xE1s tiene.",
        "Diogenes": "Di\xF3genes",
        "No man ever steps in the same river twice, for it is not the same river and he is not the same man.": "Nadie se ba\xF1a dos veces en el mismo r\xEDo, porque ni el r\xEDo ni el hombre son los mismos.",
        "Heraclitus": "Her\xE1clito",
        "Character is destiny.": "El car\xE1cter es el destino.",
        "Big results require big ambitions.": "Los grandes resultados exigen grandes ambiciones.",
        "Do not say a little in many words, but a great deal in few.": "No digas poco con muchas palabras; di mucho con pocas.",
        "Pythagoras": "Pit\xE1goras",
        "Above all things, respect yourself.": "Por encima de todo, resp\xE9tate a ti mismo.",
        "Well-being is realized by small steps, but it is truly no small thing.": "El bienestar se construye con peque\xF1os pasos, pero no es cosa peque\xF1a.",
        "Zeno": "Zen\xF3n",
        "We have two ears and one mouth, so we should listen more than we speak.": "Tenemos dos o\xEDdos y una sola boca para escuchar m\xE1s de lo que hablamos.",
        "Our doubts are traitors, and make us lose the good we oft might win by fearing to attempt.": "Nuestras dudas son traidoras: nos hacen perder el bien que podr\xEDamos ganar, por miedo a intentarlo.",
        "William Shakespeare": "William Shakespeare",
        "It is not in the stars to hold our destiny, but in ourselves.": "Nuestro destino no est\xE1 en las estrellas, sino en nosotros mismos.",
        "Wisely and slow; they stumble that run fast.": "Ve con sabidur\xEDa y despacio; tropieza el que corre deprisa.",
        "The man who is prepared has his battle half fought.": "El hombre prevenido tiene media batalla ganada.",
        "Miguel de Cervantes": "Miguel de Cervantes",
        "Diligence is the mother of good fortune.": "La diligencia es la madre de la buena fortuna.",
        "Follow your own star.": "Sigue tu propia estrella.",
        "Dante Alighieri": "Dante Alighieri",
        "There is nothing like a dream to create the future.": "No hay nada como un sue\xF1o para crear el futuro.",
        "Victor Hugo": "V\xEDctor Hugo",
        "Perseverance is the secret of all triumphs.": "La perseverancia es el secreto de todos los triunfos.",
        "Beauty will save the world.": "La belleza salvar\xE1 al mundo.",
        "Fyodor Dostoyevsky": "Fi\xF3dor Dostoievski",
        "To live without hope is to cease to live.": "Vivir sin esperanza es dejar de vivir.",
        "If you want to work on your art, work on your life.": "Si quieres trabajar en tu arte, trabaja en tu vida.",
        "Anton Chekhov": "Ant\xF3n Ch\xE9jov",
        "A thousand words leave not the same deep mark as a single deed.": "Mil palabras no dejan la huella profunda de un solo acto.",
        "Henrik Ibsen": "Henrik Ibsen",
        "Fill the unforgiving minute with sixty seconds' worth of distance run.": "Llena el minuto implacable con sesenta segundos de camino recorrido.",
        "Rudyard Kipling": "Rudyard Kipling",
        "Mark Twain": "Mark Twain",
        "Twenty years from now you will be more disappointed by the things you didn't do than by the ones you did.": "Dentro de veinte a\xF1os te decepcionar\xE1 m\xE1s lo que no hiciste que lo que hiciste.",
        "Continuous improvement is better than delayed perfection.": "La mejora continua es mejor que la perfecci\xF3n aplazada.",
        "Either write something worth reading or do something worth writing.": "O escribe algo que valga la pena leer, o haz algo que valga la pena escribir.",
        "By failing to prepare, you are preparing to fail.": "Al no prepararte, te est\xE1s preparando para fracasar.",
        "Little strokes fell great oaks.": "Peque\xF1os golpes derriban grandes robles.",
        "Theodore Roosevelt": "Theodore Roosevelt",
        "The credit belongs to the one who is actually in the arena, whose face is marred by dust and sweat.": "El m\xE9rito pertenece a quien est\xE1 de verdad en la arena, con el rostro cubierto de polvo y sudor.",
        "Believe you can and you are halfway there.": "Cree que puedes y ya habr\xE1s recorrido la mitad del camino.",
        "The most effective way to do it is to do it.": "La manera m\xE1s eficaz de hacerlo es hacerlo.",
        "Amelia Earhart": "Amelia Earhart",
        "Life is either a daring adventure or nothing at all.": "La vida es una aventura audaz o no es nada.",
        "Helen Keller": "Helen Keller",
        "Alone we can do so little; together we can do so much.": "Solos podemos hacer muy poco; juntos podemos hacer mucho.",
        "A person who never made a mistake never tried anything new.": "Una persona que nunca cometi\xF3 un error nunca intent\xF3 nada nuevo.",
        "The only source of knowledge is experience.": "La \xFAnica fuente de conocimiento es la experiencia.",
        "Strive not to be a success, but rather to be of value.": "No te esfuerces por ser un \xE9xito, sino por ser valioso.",
        "What we know is a drop; what we don't know is an ocean.": "Lo que sabemos es una gota; lo que ignoramos es un oc\xE9ano.",
        "If I have made any valuable discoveries, it has been owing more to patient attention than to any other talent.": "Si he hecho descubrimientos valiosos, se debe m\xE1s a la atenci\xF3n paciente que a cualquier otro talento.",
        "I was taught that the way of progress was neither swift nor easy.": "Me ense\xF1aron que el camino del progreso no es ni r\xE1pido ni f\xE1cil.",
        "We must have perseverance and above all confidence in ourselves.": "Debemos tener perseverancia y, sobre todo, confianza en nosotros mismos.",
        "Let me tell you the secret that has led me to my goal: my strength lies solely in my tenacity.": "D\xE9jame contarte el secreto que me llev\xF3 a mi meta: mi fuerza reside \xFAnicamente en mi tenacidad.",
        "Truth is the daughter of time, and I feel no shame in being her midwife.": "La verdad es hija del tiempo, y no me averg\xFCenza ser su partera.",
        "Johannes Kepler": "Johannes Kepler",
        "The heart has its reasons which reason knows nothing of.": "El coraz\xF3n tiene razones que la raz\xF3n no conoce.",
        "Blaise Pascal": "Blaise Pascal",
        "Truth is sought for its own sake.": "La verdad se busca por s\xED misma.",
        "Ibn al-Haytham": "Ibn al-Haytham",
        "Seek knowledge from the cradle to the grave.": "Busca el conocimiento desde la cuna hasta la tumba.",
        "Islamic tradition": "Tradici\xF3n isl\xE1mica",
        "If we all worked on the assumption that what is accepted as true is really true, there would be little hope of advance.": "Si todos asumi\xE9ramos que lo aceptado como verdadero es realmente verdadero, habr\xEDa poca esperanza de avanzar.",
        "Orville Wright": "Orville Wright",
        "It is possible to fly without motors, but not without knowledge and skill.": "Es posible volar sin motores, pero no sin conocimiento y destreza.",
        "Wilbur Wright": "Wilbur Wright",
        "That brain of mine is something more than merely mortal, as time will show.": "Esta mente m\xEDa es algo m\xE1s que meramente mortal, como el tiempo demostrar\xE1.",
        "Ada Lovelace": "Ada Lovelace",
        "However difficult life may seem, there is always something you can do and succeed at.": "Por dif\xEDcil que parezca la vida, siempre hay algo que puedes hacer y en lo que puedes triunfar.",
        "Stephen Hawking": "Stephen Hawking",
        "Look up at the stars and not down at your feet.": "Mira hacia las estrellas y no hacia tus pies.",
        "The first principle is that you must not fool yourself \u2014 and you are the easiest person to fool.": "El primer principio es que no debes enga\xF1arte a ti mismo, y t\xFA eres la persona m\xE1s f\xE1cil de enga\xF1ar.",
        "Richard Feynman": "Richard Feynman",
        "What I cannot create, I do not understand.": "Lo que no puedo crear, no lo entiendo.",
        "Somewhere, something incredible is waiting to be known.": "En alg\xFAn lugar, algo incre\xEDble espera ser conocido.",
        "Carl Sagan": "Carl Sagan",
        "Imagination will often carry us to worlds that never were. But without it we go nowhere.": "La imaginaci\xF3n nos lleva a menudo a mundos que nunca existieron. Pero sin ella no vamos a ninguna parte.",
        "Ninety-nine percent of the failures come from people who have the habit of making excuses.": "El noventa y nueve por ciento de los fracasos provienen de personas con el h\xE1bito de poner excusas.",
        "George Washington Carver": "George Washington Carver",
        "I attribute my success to this: I never gave or took any excuse.": "Atribuyo mi \xE9xito a esto: nunca di ni acept\xE9 excusas.",
        "Florence Nightingale": "Florence Nightingale",
        "Be alone; that is the secret of invention.": "Qu\xE9date a solas; ese es el secreto de la invenci\xF3n.",
        "You cannot teach a man anything; you can only help him find it within himself.": "No puedes ense\xF1arle nada a un hombre; solo puedes ayudarlo a encontrarlo dentro de s\xED mismo.",
        "Act as if what you do makes a difference. It does.": "Act\xFAa como si lo que haces marcara la diferencia. La marca.",
        "William James": "William James",
        "The greatest weapon against stress is our ability to choose one thought over another.": "El arma m\xE1s poderosa contra el estr\xE9s es nuestra capacidad de elegir un pensamiento en lugar de otro.",
        "Nothing is so fatiguing as the eternal hanging on of an uncompleted task.": "Nada cansa tanto como una tarea inconclusa que pende eternamente sobre ti.",
        "The art of being wise is the art of knowing what to overlook.": "El arte de ser sabio es el arte de saber qu\xE9 pasar por alto.",
        "Between stimulus and response there is a space. In that space is our power to choose.": "Entre el est\xEDmulo y la respuesta hay un espacio. En ese espacio est\xE1 nuestro poder de elegir.",
        "Viktor Frankl": "Viktor Frankl",
        "When we are no longer able to change a situation, we are challenged to change ourselves.": "Cuando ya no podemos cambiar una situaci\xF3n, el reto es cambiarnos a nosotros mismos.",
        "Everything can be taken from a man but one thing: the freedom to choose one's attitude.": "Al hombre se le puede quitar todo salvo una cosa: la libertad de elegir su actitud.",
        "Who looks outside, dreams; who looks inside, awakes.": "Quien mira hacia afuera, sue\xF1a; quien mira hacia adentro, despierta.",
        "Carl Jung": "Carl Jung",
        "I am not what happened to me, I am what I choose to become.": "No soy lo que me pas\xF3; soy lo que elijo llegar a ser.",
        "Until you make the unconscious conscious, it will direct your life and you will call it fate.": "Hasta que no hagas consciente lo inconsciente, dirigir\xE1 tu vida y lo llamar\xE1s destino.",
        "Do not spoil what you have by desiring what you have not.": "No arruines lo que tienes deseando lo que no tienes.",
        "Epicurus": "Epicuro",
        "Not what we have but what we enjoy constitutes our abundance.": "No lo que tenemos, sino lo que disfrutamos, constituye nuestra abundancia.",
        "Life can only be understood backwards; but it must be lived forwards.": "La vida solo puede entenderse mirando hacia atr\xE1s, pero debe vivirse hacia adelante.",
        "S\xF8ren Kierkegaard": "S\xF8ren Kierkegaard",
        "To dare is to lose one's footing momentarily. Not to dare is to lose oneself.": "Atreverse es perder el equilibrio por un momento. No atreverse es perderse a uno mismo.",
        "Ordinary people think merely of spending time; a man of talent tries to use it.": "La gente com\xFAn solo piensa en pasar el tiempo; la persona de talento intenta aprovecharlo.",
        "Arthur Schopenhauer": "Arthur Schopenhauer",
        "Health is not everything, but without health everything is nothing.": "La salud no lo es todo, pero sin salud todo es nada.",
        "The greatest thing in the world is to know how to belong to oneself.": "Lo m\xE1s grande del mundo es saber pertenecerse a uno mismo.",
        "Michel de Montaigne": "Michel de Montaigne",
        "He who fears he shall suffer, already suffers what he fears.": "Quien teme sufrir, ya sufre lo que teme.",
        "All of humanity's problems stem from man's inability to sit quietly in a room alone.": "Todos los problemas de la humanidad provienen de la incapacidad del hombre de sentarse a solas y en silencio en una habitaci\xF3n.",
        "It is not because things are difficult that we do not dare; it is because we do not dare that things are difficult.": "No es que no nos atrevamos porque las cosas sean dif\xEDciles; son dif\xEDciles porque no nos atrevemos.",
        "Patience is a tree whose root is bitter, but its fruit is sweet.": "La paciencia es un \xE1rbol de ra\xEDz amarga pero de fruto dulce.",
        "Persian proverb": "Proverbio persa",
        "This too shall pass.": "Esto tambi\xE9n pasar\xE1.",
        "Sunshine all the time makes a desert.": "El sol constante convierte la tierra en desierto.",
        "Arabic proverb": "Proverbio \xE1rabe",
        "He who wants honey must endure the sting of bees.": "Quien quiere miel debe soportar el aguij\xF3n de las abejas.",
        "Call on God, but row away from the rocks.": "Invoca a Dios, pero rema lejos de las rocas.",
        "Indian proverb": "Proverbio indio",
        "Even a sheet of paper is lighter when lifted together.": "Hasta una hoja de papel pesa menos cuando se levanta entre dos.",
        "Korean proverb": "Proverbio coreano",
        "At the end of hardship comes happiness.": "Al final de la adversidad llega la alegr\xEDa.",
        "Without effort, you cannot even pull a fish out of the pond.": "Sin esfuerzo, no sacas ni un pez del estanque.",
        "Russian proverb": "Proverbio ruso",
        "Measure seven times, cut once.": "Mide siete veces, corta una.",
        "Beginning is easy; persisting is an art.": "Empezar es f\xE1cil; perseverar es un arte.",
        "German proverb": "Proverbio alem\xE1n",
        "The morning hour has gold in its mouth.": "La hora de la ma\xF1ana lleva oro en la boca.",
        "Between saying and doing lies the sea.": "Entre el dicho y el hecho hay un mar de por medio.",
        "Italian proverb": "Proverbio italiano",
        "He who goes slowly goes safely and goes far.": "Quien va despacio, va seguro y llega lejos.",
        "You'll never plough a field by turning it over in your mind.": "Nunca arar\xE1s un campo d\xE1ndole vueltas en la cabeza.",
        "Irish proverb": "Proverbio irland\xE9s",
        "Those who wish to sing always find a song.": "Quien desea cantar siempre encuentra una canci\xF3n.",
        "Swedish proverb": "Proverbio sueco",
        "A society grows great when old men plant trees whose shade they know they shall never sit in.": "Una sociedad se vuelve grande cuando los ancianos plantan \xE1rboles bajo cuya sombra saben que nunca se sentar\xE1n.",
        "Greek proverb": "Proverbio griego",
        "Soft water strikes the hard stone until it bores through.": "Agua blanda en piedra dura, tanto golpea hasta que perfora.",
        "Portuguese proverb": "Proverbio portugu\xE9s",
        "They tried to bury us; they didn't know we were seeds.": "Quisieron enterrarnos, pero no sab\xEDan que \xE9ramos semillas.",
        "Mexican proverb": "Proverbio mexicano",
        "The soul would have no rainbow if the eyes had no tears.": "El alma no tendr\xEDa arco\xEDris si los ojos no tuvieran l\xE1grimas.",
        "Native American proverb": "Proverbio nativo americano",
        "Before enlightenment, chop wood, carry water. After enlightenment, chop wood, carry water.": "Antes de la iluminaci\xF3n, corta le\xF1a y carga agua. Despu\xE9s de la iluminaci\xF3n, corta le\xF1a y carga agua.",
        "Zen saying": "Dicho zen",
        "This is the day the Lord has made; let us rejoice and be glad in it.": "Este es el d\xEDa que hizo el Se\xF1or; alegr\xE9monos y gocemos en \xE9l.",
        "Psalm 118:24": "Salmo 118:24",
        "Weeping may endure for a night, but joy comes in the morning.": "El llanto puede durar una noche, pero la alegr\xEDa llega con la ma\xF1ana.",
        "Psalm 30:5": "Salmo 30:5",
        "Be still, and know that I am God.": "Qu\xE9date quieto y reconoce que yo soy Dios.",
        "Psalm 46:10": "Salmo 46:10",
        "Commit your way to the Lord; trust in Him, and He will act.": "Encomienda tu camino al Se\xF1or; conf\xEDa en \xC9l, y \xC9l actuar\xE1.",
        "Psalm 37:5": "Salmo 37:5",
        "The soul of the diligent shall be made rich.": "El alma del diligente ser\xE1 prosperada.",
        "Proverbs 13:4": "Proverbios 13:4",
        "A righteous man falls seven times, and rises again.": "El justo cae siete veces y vuelve a levantarse.",
        "Proverbs 24:16": "Proverbios 24:16",
        "To everything there is a season, and a time to every purpose under heaven.": "Todo tiene su tiempo, y todo lo que se quiere debajo del cielo tiene su hora.",
        "Ecclesiastes 3:1": "Eclesiast\xE9s 3:1",
        "Whoever watches the wind will not plant; whoever looks at the clouds will not reap.": "Quien observa el viento no siembra; quien mira las nubes no cosecha.",
        "Ecclesiastes 11:4": "Eclesiast\xE9s 11:4",
        "Faith by itself, if it does not have works, is dead.": "La fe, si no tiene obras, est\xE1 muerta en s\xED misma.",
        "James 2:17": "Santiago 2:17",
        "Let us not grow weary in doing good, for in due season we shall reap.": "No nos cansemos de hacer el bien, porque a su tiempo cosecharemos.",
        "Galatians 6:9": "G\xE1latas 6:9",
        "Those who wait on the Lord shall renew their strength; they shall mount up with wings like eagles.": "Los que esperan en el Se\xF1or renovar\xE1n sus fuerzas; levantar\xE1n alas como las \xE1guilas.",
        "Isaiah 40:31": "Isa\xEDas 40:31",
        "Go, sit in your cell, and your cell will teach you everything.": "Ve, si\xE9ntate en tu celda, y tu celda te lo ense\xF1ar\xE1 todo.",
        "Desert Fathers": "Padres del Desierto",
        "Start by doing what's necessary; then do what's possible; and suddenly you are doing the impossible.": "Empieza haciendo lo necesario; luego haz lo posible; y de pronto estar\xE1s haciendo lo imposible.",
        "St. Francis of Assisi": "San Francisco de As\xEDs",
        "First keep peace with yourself; then you can also bring peace to others.": "Primero mant\xE9n la paz contigo mismo; entonces podr\xE1s llevar la paz a los dem\xE1s.",
        "Thomas \xE0 Kempis": "Tom\xE1s de Kempis",
        "Faith is to believe what you do not see; the reward of this faith is to see what you believe.": "La fe es creer lo que no ves; la recompensa de esa fe es ver lo que crees.",
        "St. Augustine": "San Agust\xEDn",
        "A moment of patience in a moment of anger saves a thousand moments of regret.": "Un momento de paciencia en un momento de ira ahorra mil momentos de arrepentimiento.",
        "Ibn Qayyim al-Jawziyya": "Ibn Qayyim al-Jawziyya",
        "Do not ruin your happiness with worry, and do not ruin your mind with pessimism.": "No arruines tu felicidad con la preocupaci\xF3n, ni tu mente con el pesimismo.",
        "If you do not occupy yourself with truth, falsehood will occupy you.": "Si no te ocupas de la verdad, la falsedad se ocupar\xE1 de ti.",
        "Imam Shafi'i": "Imam Shafi'i",
        "Flowing water stays pure; standing water grows stale.": "El agua que fluye se mantiene pura; el agua estancada se corrompe.",
        "Do not let your difficulties fill you with anxiety; it is only in the darkest nights that stars shine more brightly.": "No dejes que tus dificultades te llenen de ansiedad; solo en las noches m\xE1s oscuras brillan m\xE1s las estrellas.",
        "Believe you can and you're halfway there.": "Cree que puedes y ya estar\xE1s a mitad de camino.",
        "If you're going through hell, keep going.": "Si est\xE1s atravesando el infierno, sigue adelante.",
        "Courage is what it takes to stand up and speak; courage is also what it takes to sit down and listen.": "Se necesita coraje para levantarse y hablar; tambi\xE9n se necesita coraje para sentarse y escuchar.",
        "Opportunity is missed by most people because it is dressed in overalls and looks like work.": "La mayor\xEDa deja pasar la oportunidad porque viste overol y parece trabajo.",
        "Our greatest weakness lies in giving up. The most certain way to succeed is always to try just one more time.": "Nuestra mayor debilidad es rendirnos. El camino m\xE1s seguro al \xE9xito es intentarlo siempre una vez m\xE1s.",
        "Whether you think you can, or you think you can't \u2014 you're right.": "Tanto si crees que puedes como si crees que no puedes, tienes raz\xF3n.",
        "Henry Ford": "Henry Ford",
        "The way to get started is to quit talking and begin doing.": "La manera de empezar es dejar de hablar y ponerse a hacer.",
        "Walt Disney": "Walt Disney",
        "The future belongs to those who believe in the beauty of their dreams.": "El futuro pertenece a quienes creen en la belleza de sus sue\xF1os.",
        "Eleanor Roosevelt": "Eleanor Roosevelt",
        "Do one thing every day that scares you.": "Haz cada d\xEDa algo que te d\xE9 miedo.",
        "Don't count the days; make the days count.": "No cuentes los d\xEDas; haz que los d\xEDas cuenten.",
        "Muhammad Ali": "Muhammad Ali",
        "Do not pray for an easy life; pray for the strength to endure a difficult one.": "No pidas una vida f\xE1cil; pide fuerza para soportar una vida dif\xEDcil.",
        "Bruce Lee": "Bruce Lee",
        "Be water, my friend.": "S\xE9 agua, amigo m\xEDo.",
        "Stay hungry, stay foolish.": "Sigue hambriento, sigue insensato.",
        "Steve Jobs": "Steve Jobs",
        "The only way to do great work is to love what you do.": "La \xFAnica manera de hacer un gran trabajo es amar lo que haces.",
        "This browser doesn't support background notifications. On iPhone/iPad, add the site to your Home Screen and open it from there.": "Este navegador no admite notificaciones en segundo plano. En iPhone/iPad, a\xF1ade el sitio a la pantalla de inicio y \xE1brelo desde all\xED.",
        "The background notification server isn't set up yet.": "El servidor de notificaciones en segundo plano a\xFAn no est\xE1 configurado.",
        "Sign in to your account to get notifications while the site is closed.": "Inicia sesi\xF3n en tu cuenta para recibir notificaciones con el sitio cerrado.",
        "Sign in to your account to change notification settings.": "Inicia sesi\xF3n en tu cuenta para cambiar los ajustes de notificaciones.",
        "Couldn't reach the notification server. Check your connection and try again.": "No se pudo conectar con el servidor de notificaciones. Revisa tu conexi\xF3n y vuelve a intentarlo.",
        "Your session needs refreshing. Sign out and sign in again.": "Tu sesi\xF3n necesita renovarse. Cierra sesi\xF3n y vuelve a iniciarla.",
        "Background notifications aren't ready yet. The notification setup on the server needs to be completed.": "Las notificaciones en segundo plano a\xFAn no est\xE1n listas. Falta completar la configuraci\xF3n en el servidor.",
        "Couldn't verify the notification registration for this account. Try signing in again.": "No se pudo verificar el registro de notificaciones de esta cuenta. Intenta iniciar sesi\xF3n de nuevo.",
        "Couldn't save the notification setting to the server. Try again.": "No se pudo guardar el ajuste de notificaciones en el servidor. Vuelve a intentarlo.",
        "Choose a valid time for all six notifications.": "Elige una hora v\xE1lida para las seis notificaciones.",
        "Choose a different time for each of the six notifications.": "Elige una hora distinta para cada una de las seis notificaciones.",
        "The notification service couldn't start. Refresh the page and try again.": "El servicio de notificaciones no pudo iniciarse. Actualiza la p\xE1gina y vuelve a intentarlo.",
        "Couldn't verify notification status.": "No se pudo verificar el estado de las notificaciones.",
        "Notification permission wasn't granted. You can allow it in your browser's site settings.": "No se concedi\xF3 el permiso de notificaciones. Puedes permitirlo en los ajustes del sitio de tu navegador.",
        "Couldn't close the previous device subscription. Refresh the page and try again.": "No se pudo cerrar la suscripci\xF3n anterior del dispositivo. Actualiza la p\xE1gina y vuelve a intentarlo.",
        "The signed-in account changed. Turn notifications on again from the account you're using.": "La cuenta con sesi\xF3n iniciada cambi\xF3. Vuelve a activar las notificaciones desde la cuenta que est\xE1s usando.",
        "Notifications couldn't be stopped yet. Check your connection or turn off notification permission in your browser's site settings.": "A\xFAn no se pudieron detener las notificaciones. Revisa tu conexi\xF3n o desactiva el permiso de notificaciones en los ajustes del sitio.",
        "Notifications are off on this device, but the server record couldn't be cleared. Try turning them off again when you're back online.": "Las notificaciones est\xE1n desactivadas en este dispositivo, pero no se pudo borrar el registro del servidor. Vuelve a desactivarlas cuando tengas conexi\xF3n.",
        "Server notifications are off, but the browser subscription couldn't be removed. Refresh the page and try again.": "Las notificaciones del servidor est\xE1n desactivadas, pero no se pudo eliminar la suscripci\xF3n del navegador. Actualiza la p\xE1gina y vuelve a intentarlo.",
        "The server subscription wasn't found. Turn background notifications on again.": "No se encontr\xF3 la suscripci\xF3n en el servidor. Vuelve a activar las notificaciones en segundo plano.",
        "Course lessons are currently available in Turkish.": "Por ahora, las lecciones de los cursos est\xE1n disponibles en turco.",
        "This browser can't save your progress right now. If you close the page, changes from this session may be lost.": "Este navegador no puede guardar tu progreso ahora. Si cierras la p\xE1gina, podr\xEDas perder los cambios de esta sesi\xF3n.",
        "Your progress and optional notes are stored in this browser. They are not sent to the cloud and will be lost if browser data is cleared. On a shared device, you may prefer not to leave personal notes.": "Tu progreso y tus notas opcionales se guardan en este navegador. No se env\xEDan a la nube y se perder\xE1n si se borran los datos del navegador. En un dispositivo compartido, quiz\xE1 prefieras no dejar notas personales.",
        "ODA / Guided courses": "ODA / Cursos guiados",
        "Even if you're afraid,": "Aunque tengas miedo,",
        "you can still begin.": "puedes empezar.",
        "Sometimes a quote gives you courage. Sometimes you need to see the next step together. Pick a topic and move at your own pace with short lessons.": "A veces una frase te da valor. Otras veces hace falta ver juntos el siguiente paso. Elige un tema y avanza a tu ritmo con lecciones breves.",
        "Understand": "Comprende",
        "Try": "Practica",
        "Reinforce": "Refuerza",
        "{courses} courses \xB7 {lessons} lessons": "{courses} cursos \xB7 {lessons} lecciones",
        "Content based on {count} scientific publications": "Contenido basado en {count} publicaciones cient\xEDficas",
        "Continue the course you started": "Contin\xFAa el curso que empezaste",
        "Where you left off": "Donde lo dejaste",
        "Lesson {number}": "Lecci\xF3n {number}",
        "{done}/{total} lessons completed": "{done}/{total} lecciones completadas",
        "Explore the other paths too": "Explora tambi\xE9n los otros caminos",
        "Which topic feels close to you today?": "\xBFQu\xE9 tema sientes cercano hoy?",
        "Pick a topic. Start with one small step.": "Elige un tema. Empieza con un peque\xF1o paso.",
        "{lessons} lessons \xB7 {minutes} min": "{lessons} lecciones \xB7 {minutes} min",
        "Completed \xB7 review again": "Completado \xB7 repasar",
        "{done}/{total} completed \xB7 continue": "{done}/{total} completadas \xB7 continuar",
        "Start course": "Empezar curso",
        "{title} progress": "Progreso de {title}",
        "If you're curious": "Si te da curiosidad",
        "What are these lessons based on?": "\xBFEn qu\xE9 se basan estas lecciones?",
        "Six scientific publications were reviewed before the lessons were written. Research findings were adapted into original daily exercises. ODA courses themselves have not been clinically tested; they are for education and personal practice.": "Antes de escribir las lecciones se revisaron seis publicaciones cient\xEDficas. Sus hallazgos se adaptaron a ejercicios diarios originales. Los cursos de ODA no se han probado cl\xEDnicamente; son para educaci\xF3n y pr\xE1ctica personal.",
        "Read the publication": "Leer la publicaci\xF3n",
        "All courses": "Todos los cursos",
        "Lesson {number} / {total}": "Lecci\xF3n {number} / {total}",
        "About {minutes} minutes \xB7 at your own pace": "Unos {minutes} minutos \xB7 a tu ritmo",
        "Lesson order": "Orden de lecciones",
        "Lesson {number}: {title}, completed": "Lecci\xF3n {number}: {title}, completada",
        "Lesson {number}: {title}, complete the previous lesson first": "Lecci\xF3n {number}: {title}, completa primero la lecci\xF3n anterior",
        "Lesson {number}: {title}": "Lecci\xF3n {number}: {title}",
        "This lesson's small goal": "El peque\xF1o objetivo de esta lecci\xF3n",
        "Let's try it together now. Check off each step after you try it. You can pause anytime.": "Prob\xE9moslo juntos. Marca cada paso despu\xE9s de intentarlo. Puedes hacer una pausa cuando quieras.",
        "Leaving a note is optional; you can keep your answer just for yourself.": "Dejar una nota es opcional; puedes guardarte la respuesta solo para ti.",
        "A small note to myself\u2026": "Una peque\xF1a nota para m\xED\u2026",
        "A quick check": "Una comprobaci\xF3n r\xE1pida",
        "Yes, this approach fits the goal of the lesson.": "S\xED, este enfoque encaja con el objetivo de la lecci\xF3n.",
        "Let's think about it once more.": "Pens\xE9moslo una vez m\xE1s.",
        "You can go back to the explanation and choose another answer.": "Puedes volver a la explicaci\xF3n y elegir otra respuesta.",
        "Sources and limits of this lesson": "Fuentes y l\xEDmites de esta lecci\xF3n",
        "Scientific publication": "Publicaci\xF3n cient\xEDfica",
        "Religious source": "Fuente religiosa",
        "Official health guidance": "Gu\xEDa sanitaria oficial",
        "Course completed": "Curso completado",
        "Lesson completed": "Lecci\xF3n completada",
        "What you take with you: {outcome} You can reread the lessons whenever you like.": "Lo que te llevas: {outcome} Puedes releer las lecciones cuando quieras.",
        "Go to the next lesson": "Ir a la siguiente lecci\xF3n",
        "Back to courses": "Volver a los cursos",
        "To complete the lesson, check the three practice steps and choose the right answer to the question. A personal note is optional.": "Para completar la lecci\xF3n, marca los tres pasos de pr\xE1ctica y elige la respuesta adecuada. La nota personal es opcional.",
        "Lesson completed. When you're ready, you can move to the next step.": "Lecci\xF3n completada. Cuando est\xE9s listo, puedes pasar al siguiente paso.",
        "Complete lesson": "Completar lecci\xF3n",
        "The operation was stopped.": "Operaci\xF3n detenida.",
        "Your device couldn't free up enough memory for the AI. Close other tabs and try restarting the coach.": "Tu dispositivo no pudo liberar suficiente memoria para la IA. Cierra otras pesta\xF1as e intenta reiniciar el coach.",
        "The model files couldn't be loaded. Check your internet connection and your browser's free storage, then try again.": "No se pudieron cargar los archivos del modelo. Revisa tu conexi\xF3n a internet y el espacio libre del navegador, y vuelve a intentarlo.",
        "This browser or device doesn't support the AI engine. Try again in an up-to-date browser with WebGPU support.": "Este navegador o dispositivo no admite el motor de IA. Vuelve a intentarlo en un navegador actualizado con WebGPU.",
        "The AI couldn't finish its reply. Restart the coach and try again.": "La IA no pudo terminar su respuesta. Reinicia el coach y vuelve a intentarlo.",
        "The live coach needs an up-to-date browser with WebGPU support.": "El coach en vivo necesita un navegador actualizado con WebGPU.",
        "Open the live coach from the site's secure HTTPS address.": "Abre el coach en vivo desde la direcci\xF3n HTTPS segura del sitio.",
        "WebGPU isn't available in this browser. Try again with an up-to-date Chrome or Edge.": "WebGPU no est\xE1 disponible en este navegador. Vuelve a intentarlo con Chrome o Edge actualizados.",
        "Couldn't access the graphics card. Turn on hardware acceleration in your browser and try again.": "No se pudo acceder a la tarjeta gr\xE1fica. Activa la aceleraci\xF3n por hardware del navegador y vuelve a intentarlo.",
        "The browser couldn't access the graphics card. Try another up-to-date browser with WebGPU support.": "El navegador no pudo acceder a la tarjeta gr\xE1fica. Prueba con otro navegador actualizado con WebGPU.",
        "Write a message to send to the coach.": "Escribe un mensaje para enviarlo al coach.",
        "The AI engine stopped. Restart the coach and try again.": "El motor de IA se detuvo. Reinicia el coach y vuelve a intentarlo.",
        "Model ready.": "Modelo listo.",
        "Checking device compatibility\u2026": "Comprobando la compatibilidad del dispositivo\u2026",
        "The live coach isn't supported on this device.": "El coach en vivo no es compatible con este dispositivo.",
        "The coach is ready. You can start talking.": "El coach est\xE1 listo. Puedes empezar a conversar.",
        "Start the live coach first.": "Primero inicia el coach en vivo.",
        "Wait for the previous reply to finish or stop it.": "Espera a que termine la respuesta anterior o detenla.",
        "The coach couldn't create a reply this time. You can send your message again.": "El coach no pudo crear una respuesta esta vez. Puedes volver a enviar tu mensaje.",
        "Downloading and preparing the model \xB7 {percent}%": "Descargando y preparando el modelo \xB7 {percent} %",
        "Daily check-in recorded. +D$50": "Registro diario guardado. +D$50",
        "Tab title blink is on.": "El parpadeo del t\xEDtulo de la pesta\xF1a est\xE1 activado.",
        "Tab title blink is off.": "El parpadeo del t\xEDtulo de la pesta\xF1a est\xE1 desactivado.",
        "Screen edge pulse is on.": "El pulso del borde de pantalla est\xE1 activado.",
        "Screen edge pulse is off.": "El pulso del borde de pantalla est\xE1 desactivado.",
        "Previewing the finish alert for 5 seconds.": "Vista previa de la alerta de fin durante 5 segundos.",
        "Plan saved. You know what to do when it gets hard.": "Plan guardado. Ya sabes qu\xE9 hacer cuando se ponga dif\xEDcil.",
        "Make it doable": "Hazlo posible",
        "Your plan for today": "Tu plan para hoy",
        "Thirty seconds now saves you from deciding again later.": "Treinta segundos ahora te ahorran volver a decidir m\xE1s tarde.",
        "1. How does this decision feel right now?": "1. \xBFC\xF3mo te hace sentir esta decisi\xF3n ahora mismo?",
        "Rewrite it smaller (optional)": "Reescr\xEDbela m\xE1s peque\xF1a (opcional)",
        "2. What could stop you today?": "2. \xBFQu\xE9 podr\xEDa frenarte hoy?",
        "e.g. I\u2019ll pick up my phone first": "p. ej., agarrar\xE9 el m\xF3vil primero",
        "3. If that happens, I will\u2026": "3. Si eso pasa, yo\u2026",
        "e.g. put the phone in another room and start for two minutes": "p. ej., dejar\xE9 el m\xF3vil en otra habitaci\xF3n y empezar\xE9 dos minutos",
        "Deciding in advance what you will do when the obstacle appears is one of the best-studied ways to follow through.": "Decidir de antemano qu\xE9 har\xE1s cuando aparezca el obst\xE1culo es una de las formas m\xE1s estudiadas de cumplir lo que te propones.",
        "Save plan": "Guardar plan",
        "Make it real": "Hazlo real",
        "Picturing a dream feels good, but on its own it can drain the energy to act. Name what\u2019s in the way, then take one small step.": "Imaginar un sue\xF1o se siente bien, pero por s\xED solo puede quitarte energ\xEDa para actuar. Nombra lo que se interpone y da un peque\xF1o paso.",
        "What stands between you and this?": "\xBFQu\xE9 se interpone entre t\xFA y esto?",
        "Your next small step": "Tu siguiente peque\xF1o paso",
        "Make it today\u2019s decision": "Convi\xE9rtelo en la decisi\xF3n de hoy",
        "You already have a decision for today. Save this step for tomorrow.": "Ya tienes una decisi\xF3n para hoy. Guarda este paso para ma\xF1ana.",
        "Yesterday didn\u2019t happen. That\u2019s okay.": "Ayer no sali\xF3. Est\xE1 bien.",
        "Welcome back. Today is a clean page.": "Bienvenido de nuevo. Hoy es una p\xE1gina en blanco.",
        "A new month, a clean page.": "Un mes nuevo, una p\xE1gina en blanco.",
        "A new week, a clean page.": "Una semana nueva, una p\xE1gina en blanco.",
        "Missing one day doesn\u2019t undo your progress. What matters is not missing twice. Choose the smallest version of today\u2019s decision.": "Fallar un d\xEDa no borra tu progreso. Lo importante es no fallar dos veces. Elige la versi\xF3n m\xE1s peque\xF1a de la decisi\xF3n de hoy.",
        "No need to make up for the missed days. Go easy on yourself about the gap, and choose one small decision for today.": "No hace falta recuperar los d\xEDas perdidos. S\xE9 amable contigo por la pausa y elige una peque\xF1a decisi\xF3n para hoy.",
        "New beginnings make change easier to start. What do you want this period to be about? Begin with today\u2019s decision.": "Los nuevos comienzos facilitan empezar a cambiar. \xBFDe qu\xE9 quieres que trate esta etapa? Empieza con la decisi\xF3n de hoy.",
        "Make it smaller": "Hazla m\xE1s peque\xF1a",
        "Choose today\u2019s decision": "Elige la decisi\xF3n de hoy",
        "Your evidence starts today": "Tus pruebas empiezan hoy",
        "1 kept promise": "1 promesa cumplida",
        "{n} kept promises": "{n} promesas cumplidas",
        "This week: {n} of 7 days": "Esta semana: {n} de 7 d\xEDas",
        "A simple start": "Un comienzo sencillo",
        "For your first week you\u2019ll see only what matters most: one decision a day. The other tools open after {n} kept decisions.": "En tu primera semana ver\xE1s solo lo m\xE1s importante: una decisi\xF3n al d\xEDa. Las dem\xE1s herramientas se abren tras cumplir {n} decisiones.",
        "Show everything now": "Mostrar todo ahora",
        "A little": "Un poco",
        "Not yet": "Todav\xEDa no",
        "Did you start something you had been putting off?": "\xBFEmpezaste algo que ven\xEDas posponiendo?",
        "Days since start: {n}": "D\xEDas desde el inicio: {n}",
        "Decisions set: {n}": "Decisiones fijadas: {n}",
        "Decisions kept: {n}": "Decisiones cumplidas: {n}",
        "Plans made: {n}": "Planes hechos: {n}",
        "Two-minute starts: {n}": "Inicios de dos minutos: {n}",
        "Thank you. This helps us make ODA better.": "Gracias. Esto nos ayuda a mejorar ODA.",
        "Two weeks in": "Dos semanas despu\xE9s",
        "What helped, or what got in the way? (optional)": "\xBFQu\xE9 te ayud\xF3 o qu\xE9 te lo impidi\xF3? (opcional)",
        "Send to the ODA team": "Enviar al equipo de ODA",
        "Just save": "Solo guardar",
        "Sending opens your email app with your answer and a few usage numbers. Nothing is sent automatically.": "Enviar abre tu app de correo con tu respuesta y algunos datos de uso. No se env\xEDa nada autom\xE1ticamente.",
        "You started.": "Empezaste.",
        "Just two minutes": "Solo dos minutos",
        "That was the hardest part. Stop here with a clear conscience, or keep going while you\u2019re warm.": "Eso era lo m\xE1s dif\xEDcil. Para aqu\xED con la conciencia tranquila o sigue mientras est\xE1s en marcha.",
        "You don\u2019t have to finish. Just start \u201C{title}\u201D. When the time is up, you may stop.": "No tienes que terminar. Solo empieza \u201C{title}\u201D. Cuando acabe el tiempo, puedes parar.",
        "{time} left": "Quedan {time}",
        "Two minutes are up.": "Se acabaron los dos minutos.",
        "I did it \u2014 mark as done": "Lo hice: marcar como hecha",
        "Keep going with a focus timer": "Seguir con un temporizador de enfoque",
        "Stop for now": "Parar por ahora",
        "Today I decided: \u201C{title}\u201D. Ask me tonight if I did it.": "Hoy decid\xED: \u201C{title}\u201D. Preg\xFAntame esta noche si lo hice.",
        "Evidence": "Pruebas",
        "Proof that you keep your word": "La prueba de que cumples tu palabra",
        "Once already, you did what you said you would. That is who you are becoming.": "Ya una vez hiciste lo que dijiste que har\xEDas. Esa es la persona en la que te est\xE1s convirtiendo.",
        "{n} times you did what you said you would. That is who you are becoming.": "{n} veces hiciste lo que dijiste que har\xEDas. Esa es la persona en la que te est\xE1s convirtiendo.",
        "Every decision you keep will be written here. Motivation often follows action, and this list is how you\u2019ll see it.": "Cada decisi\xF3n que cumplas quedar\xE1 escrita aqu\xED. La motivaci\xF3n suele llegar despu\xE9s de la acci\xF3n, y aqu\xED lo ver\xE1s.",
        "Kept decisions": "Decisiones cumplidas",
        "Days with a kept decision": "D\xEDas con una decisi\xF3n cumplida",
        "Go to today\u2019s decision": "Ir a la decisi\xF3n de hoy",
        "with a plan": "con un plan",
        "started with 2 minutes": "empezada con 2 minutos",
        "Your evidence": "Tus pruebas",
        "Every decision you kept": "Cada decisi\xF3n que cumpliste",
        "Copied. Send it to one person you trust.": "Copiado. Env\xEDalo a una persona de confianza.",
        "Sharing isn\u2019t available here.": "Compartir no est\xE1 disponible aqu\xED.",
        "If {obstacle}": "Si {obstacle}",
        "If it gets hard": "Si se pone dif\xEDcil",
        "then I will {plan}": "entonces: {plan}",
        "That\u2019s proof #{n} that you keep your word.": "Es la prueba n.\xBA {n} de que cumples tu palabra.",
        "Start \xB7 just 2 minutes": "Empieza \xB7 solo 2 minutos",
        "Plan for obstacles \xB7 30 sec": "Planifica los obst\xE1culos \xB7 30 s",
        "Tell one person": "Cu\xE9ntaselo a alguien",
        "Too big": "Demasiado grande",
        "Make it smaller. What is the first piece you could finish in two minutes?": "Hazla m\xE1s peque\xF1a. \xBFCu\xE1l es la primera parte que podr\xEDas terminar en dos minutos?",
        "Boring": "Aburrida",
        "Boring is allowed. Pair it with something you enjoy, or promise yourself only two minutes.": "Est\xE1 bien que sea aburrida. Comb\xEDnala con algo que disfrutes o prom\xE9tete solo dos minutos.",
        "Scary": "Da miedo",
        "Fear often means it matters. You don\u2019t need to feel ready to take one small step.": "El miedo suele indicar que importa. No necesitas sentirte listo para dar un peque\xF1o paso.",
        "Unclear": "Poco clara",
